# ds18-bridge .gitignore
#
# Philosophy: this repository's value is the measurement dataset, the tune library and the
# DSB knowledge base. Those are all tracked. What is excluded is either build output,
# a cache, or something that can be fetched again.
#
# The nested clone at evidence\caraudio1\upstream is deliberately excluded: it carries its
# own .git and is one `git clone` away from being whole. Git treats an embedded .git as a
# gitlink and silently records a commit hash instead of the files - the worst of both.
# Everything from that repo that this project actually relies on is either vendored in
# evidence\caraudio1\repo\ or quoted in DSB\refs\.

# --- build output (regenerated by build.ps1 / build-rta.ps1 / build-sweep.ps1 / app\build.ps1)
bin/
app/bin/
app/obj/
*.exe
*.dll
!vendor/*.dll
*.pdb

# --- the re-fetchable external clone
evidence/caraudio1/upstream/

# --- caches and bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- the verify gate's own state, regenerated by every run
.opencode/verify-state.json

# --- OS and editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# --- NOT ignored, on purpose:
#   measurements\*.wav    the primary dataset; losing it loses the project
#   evidence\*.wav        raw capture evidence referenced by STATE.md
#   banks\*.idsp          the tune library (12 files)
#   web\*.idsp            tunes the app serves
#   DSB\                  the whole knowledge base
#   targets.json          live data the bridge API serves
#   *.log                 build logs are evidence of what was tried
